Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 18:23:10 +0200
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: read each register into its own word over MDIO

qca8k_bulk_read() is the regmap read op. When the Ethernet management
path is not available it falls back to reading the registers one by one
over MDIO, but it stores register i at val_buf + i with val_buf a void
pointer: the words land one byte apart and overwrite each other, and the
last three bytes of a three-register read are never written.

Every multi-register read over MDIO is garbage then - the ATU entry in
qca8k_fdb_read() above all: the dump shows MACs made of the VID and the
aging field, FDB_NEXT never moves past it, and a search reads a wrong
status and port mask for the entry it found. With tag_qca the
management frames carry these reads and the fallback is rarely taken;
with a tagger that has no management frames it is taken every time.

Store each register in its own u32.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@ qca8k_bulk_read(void *ctx, const void *r
 
 	/* loop count times and increment reg of 4 */
 	for (i = 0; i < count; i++, reg += sizeof(u32)) {
-		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, val_buf + i);
+		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, (u32 *)val_buf + i);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 	}
